course: dictionary
lesson: 10528
title: Meet the tyrant lizard king
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A dinosaur can have a long full name and a short name. Tyrannosaurus rex is the full name, and people often shorten it to T. rex. «Tyrannosaurus rex lived about 68 to 66 million years ago in western North America.» Both names point to the same huge dinosaur.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Tyrannosaurus had long, sharp, curved teeth for meat» tells you it ate meat. «A grown one was about 12 metres long and as tall at the hips as a double-decker bus» tells you it was enormous. Put the clues together and you can picture it.
explain: Scientists learn about tyrannosaurus from fossils, the bones and teeth that have turned to stone. «By looking at a fossil skull, scientists can tell what an animal ate.» When you meet a new word in science, use the clues around it, then check in a dictionary.
fact: A tyrannosaurus is a huge meat-eating dinosaur.
fact: It walked on two strong back legs and had tiny front arms.
fact: «Tyrannosaurus rex» means «tyrant lizard king» in its name.
fact: Its teeth could be up to about 30 centimetres long, with the root, and able to crush bone.
fact: «T. rex» is the short way to write Tyrannosaurus rex.
exercise: «Tyrannosaurus had long, sharp, curved teeth for meat.» What did it eat? | *Meat | Plants | Insects only | Seeds
exercise: Find and copy the short name for Tyrannosaurus rex. | fossil | metres | *T. rex | Triceratops
exercise: A grown tyrannosaurus was about how long? | About 30 metres long | *About 12 metres long | About 12 centimetres long | About 1 metre long
test: «Tyrannosaurus rex lived about 68 to 66 million years ago.» When did it live compared with people? | *Long before people existed | After every person was born | At the same time as the first cities | Only a few hundred years ago
test: Which description fits a tyrannosaurus? | A small lizard that flies over the sea | A fossil found in a museum shop | *A huge meat-eating dinosaur with tiny front arms | A plant-eating dinosaur with a beak
exam: What do the teeth of a tyrannosaurus show about it? | *It was built to eat meat, with large teeth able to crush bone | It ate plants like a Triceratops | It had no teeth at all | It had a beak and grinding teeth
